bio-long-read-splicing,"Analyzes alternative splicing from PacBio Iso-Seq (HiFi, Kinnex/MAS-Iso-seq) and Oxford Nanopore (direct cDNA, direct RNA, R10.4.1+) long-read RNA-seq with full-isoform resolution. Tools include FLAIR (correct/collapse/quantify/diffSplice for PacBio + ONT), IsoQuant (de-novo or annotation-guided isoform discovery 2024 SOTA), Bambu (annotation-aware Bayesian discovery + quantification with Novel Discovery Rate), SQANTI3 (isoform classification: FSM/ISM/NIC/NNC + artifact flags), rMATS-long (event calling on long-read isoforms), and minimap2 (-ax splice:hq for HiFi; -ax splice -k14 for ONT cDNA; add -uf only for direct RNA or stranded cDNA preps). Solves microexon detection, recursive splicing, complex multi-exon isoforms, and DTU without transcript-quantification uncertainty. Use when short-read AS limitations (anchor length, complex isoforms, microexons, recursive splicing, transcript ambiguity) demand full-isoform resolution.",GPTomics,bioSkills,1114,search_rank=255,search,https://github.com/GPTomics/bioSkills,https://github.com/GPTomics/bioSkills/blob/HEAD/alternative-splicing/long-read-splicing/SKILL.md,GPTomics/bioSkills/alternative-splicing/long-read-splicing/SKILL.md,1,,0,,bb8f50351260e2011de7f981e27e27fde484a40a,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""ssw-py"", ""ecosystem"": ""pip"", ""install_command"": ""| `IsoQuant: ssw-py not found` | Missing dependency | `pip install ssw-py` |""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""ssw-py"", ""ecosystem"": ""pip"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
bio-workflows-metabolic-modeling-pipeline,"Orchestrates genome-scale metabolic modeling from a protein FASTA to flux predictions, chaining CarveMe/gapseq reconstruction, memote QC, gap-filling, media-constrained FBA/FVA, gene essentiality, and context-specific models. Use when committing the reconstruction tool (which locks the identifier NAMESPACE forever - BiGG vs ModelSEED vs KEGG, no automatic translation), setting the medium BEFORE FBA (the exchange bounds ARE the medium; essentiality and gap-fill are computed relative to it), curating iteratively (stoichiometric-consistency first, then mass/charge, then directionality, then GPR) with energy-generating-cycle removal, and reading a MEMOTE score as well-formedness NOT correctness. Hands mechanism to the systems-biology component skills; not a re-teach of any single step.",GPTomics,bioSkills,1114,search_rank=255,search,https://github.com/GPTomics/bioSkills,https://github.com/GPTomics/bioSkills/blob/HEAD/workflows/metabolic-modeling-pipeline/SKILL.md,GPTomics/bioSkills/workflows/metabolic-modeling-pipeline/SKILL.md,1,,0,,6b9f61c141dc8b5e1930a63ff849397290b97ce3,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""pandas"", ""ecosystem"": ""pip"", ""install_command"": ""pip install cobra carveme memote escher pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn""}]",C,"[{""package"": ""pandas"", ""ecosystem"": ""pip"", ""vuln_count"": 1, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": [""PYSEC-2020-73""]}]"
