browser-mcp-agent,"Give an AI agent its own real browser over MCP tool calls - launch, navigate, click, fill, screenshot, extract text, run JS - with a kernel-level real-device fingerprint and a persistent profile, so the session stays logged in between runs and pages see one coherent device instead of a headless build. No Playwright or SDK code to write. Use when an agent should operate a site itself, when a computer-use / browser-use setup needs a captured real fingerprint rather than a synthetic one, when agent sessions keep losing their login, or when comparing hosted agent-browser services. Also for 'MCP browser', 'browser MCP server', 'let my agent browse the web', 'agent browser control', 'browser-use MCP', 'computer use browser', 'Browserbase alternative', 'Steel browser alternative', 'headless browser detected'. Node (npx) or Python; Windows x64, macOS Intel + Apple Silicon, Linux x64 / arm64. SDK and REST reference is anti-detect-browser; account isolation is multi-account-isolation.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/antibrow/anti-detect-browser-skills/browser-mcp-agent/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/antibrow/anti-detect-browser-skills/browser-mcp-agent/SKILL.md,1,,1,antibrow/anti-detect-browser-skills,5fd1539ff41deeea98441ac259b2ac90b4b1e8b9,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""anti-detect-browser"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""- **The version is pinned.** Bare `npx anti-detect-browser` resolves `latest` from the npm registry on every start, so the code that runs is whatever was published most recently. Pinning turns it into""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""anti-detect-browser"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
browser-navigator,"Automates browser actions using Playwright CLI. Can record, replay, and generate browser automation scenarios stored in the knowledge base. Useful for UI testing, data extraction, and visual auditing.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/famaoai-creator/gemini-skills/browser-navigator/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/famaoai-creator/gemini-skills/browser-navigator/SKILL.md,1,,0,,d6e5c613b642c7cd38f3122622a4c62d92bd7b1e,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""@playwright/test"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""- **Environment**: If Playwright is not installed, prompt the user to run `npm install -D @playwright/test`.""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""@playwright/test"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
browser-trace,"Capture a full DevTools-protocol trace of any browser automation — CDP firehose, screenshots, and DOM dumps — then bisect the stream into per-page searchable buckets. Use when the user wants to debug a failed run, audit network/console/DOM activity, attach a trace to an in-progress session, or feed structured per-page summaries back into an agent loop so its next iteration learns from the last one.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/browserbase/skills/browser-trace/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/browserbase/skills/browser-trace/SKILL.md,1,,1,browserbase/skills,9911f9b4b136e6be858fc2c3640e87b29bc01fed,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""@browserbasehq/browse-cli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""compatibility: \""Requires Node 18+, the browse CLI (`npm install -g @browserbasehq/browse-cli@alpha` or 0.5.1+ once released — `browse cdp` is alpha-tagged), and optionally `jq` for ad-hoc querying of ""}, {""package"": ""@browserbasehq/cli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""compatibility: \""Requires Node 18+, the browse CLI (`npm install -g @browserbasehq/browse-cli@alpha` or 0.5.1+ once released — `browse cdp` is alpha-tagged), and optionally `jq` for ad-hoc querying of ""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""@browserbasehq/browse-cli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}, {""package"": ""@browserbasehq/cli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
browserbase-cli,"Use the Browserbase CLI (`bb`) for Browserbase Functions and platform API workflows. Use when the user asks to run `bb`, deploy or invoke functions, manage sessions, projects, contexts, or extensions, fetch a page through the Browserbase Fetch API, search the web through the Browserbase Search API, or open the Browserbase dashboard from the command line. Prefer the Browser skill for interactive browsing; use `bb browse` only when the user explicitly wants the Browserbase CLI path.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/browserbase/skills/browserbase-cli/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/browserbase/skills/browserbase-cli/SKILL.md,1,,1,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,1dafbb0ff21dfb0014181ad0e6574c6cfb9ea5bd,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""@browserbasehq/browse-cli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""- `bb browse` install error: run `npm install -g @browserbasehq/browse-cli`""}, {""package"": ""@browserbasehq/cli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""compatibility: \""Requires the Browserbase CLI (`npm install -g @browserbasehq/cli`). API commands require `BROWSERBASE_API_KEY`. `BROWSERBASE_PROJECT_ID` is only needed for `bb functions dev` and `bb f""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""@browserbasehq/browse-cli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}, {""package"": ""@browserbasehq/cli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
