codex-cli-specialist,"This skill should be used when the user asks to ""set up Codex CLI"", ""convert skills for Codex"", ""write cross-platform AI skills"", ""configure agents/openai.yaml"", ""build skills index"", ""validate skill compatibility"", ""sync skills between Claude Code and Codex"", or ""optimize Codex CLI workflows"". Use for OpenAI Codex CLI mastery, cross-platform skill authoring, skill conversion, and multi-agent compatibility patterns.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/borghei/claude-skills/codex-cli-specialist/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/borghei/claude-skills/codex-cli-specialist/SKILL.md,1,,1,borghei/claude-skills,c49f2dbf46a858b736b78f120811287bbeffb9aa,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""@openai/codex"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""npm install -g @openai/codex""}]",C,"[{""package"": ""@openai/codex"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 2, ""max_severity"": ""CRITICAL"", ""advisory_ids"": [""GHSA-w5fx-fh39-j5rw"", ""GHSA-xrxf-jgv3-qmrm""]}]"
codex-code-review,"Perform comprehensive code reviews using OpenAI Codex CLI. This skill should be used when users request code reviews, want to analyze diffs/PRs, need security audits, performance analysis, or want automated code quality feedback. Supports reviewing staged changes, specific files, entire directories, or git diffs.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/tyrchen/claude-skills/codex-code-review/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/tyrchen/claude-skills/codex-code-review/SKILL.md,1,,0,,b4ffd1bcc64c77a0f800a8f1feed4681105e23f7,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""@openai/codex"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""npm install -g @openai/codex""}]",C,"[{""package"": ""@openai/codex"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 2, ""max_severity"": ""CRITICAL"", ""advisory_ids"": [""GHSA-w5fx-fh39-j5rw"", ""GHSA-xrxf-jgv3-qmrm""]}]"
codex-delegate,"Delegate a coding task to the OpenAI Codex CLI as a background implementer, then review its diff and land it yourself. Use this whenever the user wants to hand implementation work to Codex — phrasings like ""have Codex do X"", ""delegate this to Codex"", ""run it through Codex"", or ""use Codex to implement/fix/refactor"" — or wants to run a queue of coding tasks through Codex while staying the reviewer. Prefer it over a one-shot Codex forwarder (such as the codex-rescue agent) specifically when the user will review the resulting diff and commit it themselves, or wants the full brief → dispatch → review → commit loop across a single task or a queue. Also reach for it proactively for a separate implementation pass on a bounded, well-specified task (an implementation sweep, a migration, a mechanical refactor, parallel work). Covers writing the Codex brief, dispatching it via the bundled relay.mjs helper, waiting for completion, reviewing the result, and committing. DO NOT USE for tasks small enough to do inline, or when the user wants the code written directly without delegating.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/amelnagdy/delegate-skills/codex-delegate/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/amelnagdy/delegate-skills/codex-delegate/SKILL.md,1,,1,amelnagdy/delegate-skills,d2d39d6586e962b2de83325b6690e38bb878e8bd,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""@openai/codex"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""1. `codex --version` succeeds. If not, install (`npm i -g @openai/codex`) and `codex login`.""}]",C,"[{""package"": ""@openai/codex"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 2, ""max_severity"": ""CRITICAL"", ""advisory_ids"": [""GHSA-w5fx-fh39-j5rw"", ""GHSA-xrxf-jgv3-qmrm""]}]"
