github-repository-architect,"Complete GitHub repository setup with production-grade standards including community health files, CI/CD workflows, issue templates, documentation site, badges, CODEOWNERS, and release management. Handles initialization, configuration, GitHub Pages deployment, and automated quality checks for professional open-source or enterprise projects.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/hummbl-dev/hummbl-claude-skills/github-repository-architect/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/hummbl-dev/hummbl-claude-skills/github-repository-architect/SKILL.md,1,,0,,49213ebb72cf0c86397a08ba4dc2478c8cfa0281,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""mkdocs"", ""ecosystem"": ""pip"", ""install_command"": ""1. Install: `pip install mkdocs mkdocs-material`""}]",C,"[{""package"": ""mkdocs"", ""ecosystem"": ""pip"", ""vuln_count"": 2, ""max_severity"": ""HIGH"", ""advisory_ids"": [""GHSA-qh9q-34h6-hcv9"", ""PYSEC-2021-878""]}]"
github-upload-image-to-pr,"Upload local images to a GitHub PR and embed them in the description or comments. Use when asked to ""attach screenshots to PR"", ""add images to PR"", ""upload test results to PR"", ""embed screenshots in PR description"", ""add before/after images to PR"", ""attach UI screenshots"", ""show test results in PR"", ""add visual evidence to PR"", or any request involving images and PRs. Always use this skill when the user wants to visually document changes in a pull request, even if they don't use the word ""upload"" — phrases like ""put the screenshot in the PR"" or ""show the image in the PR"" should trigger this skill. Supports Playwright MCP / Chrome DevTools MCP / agent-browser as browser automation backends.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/tonkotsuboy/github-upload-image-to-pr/github-upload-image-to-pr/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/tonkotsuboy/github-upload-image-to-pr/github-upload-image-to-pr/SKILL.md,1,,0,,9704de46a9389a8c2bf61fc0f258339a00e1c274,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""agent-browser"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""| agent-browser not found | `npm install -g agent-browser && agent-browser install` |""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""agent-browser"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
github-upload-media-to-pr,"Upload local images and videos to a GitHub PR and embed them in the description or comments. Use when asked to ""attach screenshots to PR"", ""add images to PR"", ""upload test results to PR"", ""embed screenshots in PR description"", ""add before/after images to PR"", ""attach UI screenshots"", ""show test results in PR"", ""add visual evidence to PR"", ""attach video to PR"", ""upload recording to PR"", ""add demo video to PR"", or any request involving media and PRs. Always use this skill when the user wants to visually document changes in a pull request, even if they don't use the word ""upload"" — phrases like ""put the screenshot in the PR"" or ""show the recording in the PR"" should trigger this skill. Supports images (png, jpg, gif, webp) and videos (mp4, webm, mov). Uses agent-browser (vercel-labs/agent-browser) for browser automation.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/jacobmassey/github-upload-media-to-pr/github-upload-media-to-pr/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/jacobmassey/github-upload-media-to-pr/github-upload-media-to-pr/SKILL.md,1,,0,,ebdf7744bb68debb26cf3fda9b0b45d6cab062ea,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""agent-browser"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""If not found, install it: `npm i -g agent-browser && agent-browser install`""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""agent-browser"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
