opencli,"OpenCLI — Make any website your CLI. Zero risk, AI-powered, reuse Chrome login.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/jackwener/opencli/opencli/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/jackwener/opencli/opencli/SKILL.md,1,,3,"NeverSight/learn-skills.dev, openakita/openakita",0ba55dbd52b0da2d3c7ac3ad5d454e25385806cf,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""@jackwener/opencli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""npm install -g @jackwener/opencli""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""@jackwener/opencli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
opencli-reader,"Generic read-only fallback for any source opencli covers but this repo has no dedicated reader for — Yahoo Finance, Bloomberg, Reuters, Barchart, Eastmoney, Xueqiu, Sinafinance, Reddit, HackerNews, Substack, Medium, Weibo, Bilibili, Xiaohongshu, Zhihu, arXiv, Google Scholar, Apple Podcasts, Xiaoyuzhou, Spotify, YouTube, Weixin, Amazon, and more. Triggers: ""use opencli to read"", ""grab the frontpage from hackernews"", ""read reddit r/wallstreetbets"", ""fetch Eastmoney hot stocks"", ""pull Xueqiu feed"", ""get Bloomberg markets headlines"", ""search arXiv for"", any request to read from a site where a specialized skill does not exist but opencli does. FALLBACK — prefer twitter-reader, linkedin-reader, discord-reader, telegram-reader, or yc-reader when the source matches. READ-ONLY — never invoke write operations.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/himself65/finance-skills/opencli-reader/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/himself65/finance-skills/opencli-reader/SKILL.md,1,,0,,d7ab59dac8e316538bfe464d4888f6a9078ce921,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""@jackwener/opencli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""npm install -g @jackwener/opencli""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""@jackwener/opencli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
opencli-universal-cli-hub,"Convert websites, Electron apps, and local tools into standardized CLIs for AI agents and humans using OpenCLI's browser automation and adapter framework.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/aradotso/devtools-skills/opencli-universal-cli-hub/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/aradotso/devtools-skills/opencli-universal-cli-hub/SKILL.md,1,,0,,f338f8101b30defd71d9c09a158d975d68b3006a,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""@jackwener/opencli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""npm install -g @jackwener/opencli""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""@jackwener/opencli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
opencli-usage,"Use at the start of any OpenCLI session — this is the top-level map of what `opencli` can do, how to discover adapters, what flags and output formats are universal, and which specialized skill to load next. Point here when an agent asks ""what can opencli do?"" or ""how do I find the right command?"".",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/ownduck/opencli/opencli-usage/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/ownduck/opencli/opencli-usage/SKILL.md,1,,1,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,7b7e4f4e2d504ef0ee9bb5390f30c7856fc324c6,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""@jackwener/opencli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""npm install -g @jackwener/opencli          # binary: opencli, requires Node >= 21""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""@jackwener/opencli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
opencli-usage,"Use when running OpenCLI commands to interact with websites (Bilibili, Twitter, Reddit, Xiaohongshu, etc.), desktop apps (Cursor, Notion), or public APIs (HackerNews, arXiv). Covers installation, command reference, and output formats for 73+ adapters.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/jackwener/opencli/opencli-usage/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/jackwener/opencli/opencli-usage/SKILL.md,1,,1,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,e4138f40aadfb3f217e8b2772e1572e5c416775d,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""@jackwener/opencli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""npm install -g @jackwener/opencli""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""@jackwener/opencli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
opencode,"Expert guide for working with opencode.ai - TUI commands, CLI operations, custom commands, agents, tools, skills system, and AGENTS.md configuration",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/dimitrigilbert/ai-skills/opencode/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/dimitrigilbert/ai-skills/opencode/SKILL.md,1,,2,"nousresearch/hermes-agent, volcengine/OpenViking",d4ff78c5cc3107c847c85a816b98852718ffed8e,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""opencode-ai"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""npm install -g opencode-ai""}]",C,"[{""package"": ""opencode-ai"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 2, ""max_severity"": ""CRITICAL"", ""advisory_ids"": [""GHSA-c83v-7274-4vgp"", ""GHSA-vxw4-wv6m-9hhh""]}]"
opencode-agents,"Delegate tasks to oh-my-openagent agents (librarian, oracle, sisyphus, prometheus, atlas, explore, metis, momus) via the oh-my-opencode CLI. Use this skill whenever the user says 'use librarian to', 'use oracle to', 'let librarian', 'ask oracle to', '@librarian', '@oracle', or names any oh-my-openagent agent in the context of doing a task. Also triggers on Chinese equivalents: '用 librarian 做', '用 oracle 做', '让 librarian 帮'. Disambiguation: do NOT trigger for Oracle Database, Oracle Cloud, MongoDB Atlas, or general-purpose exploration verbs unrelated to oh-my-openagent.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/axot/agent-skills/opencode-agents/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/axot/agent-skills/opencode-agents/SKILL.md,1,,0,,e77e9c60ea64d87ca1fc51e668691e2de4eb6e5b,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""oh-my-opencode"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""- **If `oh-my-opencode` is not in PATH**: report the error clearly and suggest installing via `npm install -g oh-my-opencode`""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""oh-my-opencode"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
opencode-delegate,"Delegate a coding task to the OpenCode CLI as a background implementer, then review its diff and land it yourself. Use this whenever the user wants to hand implementation work to OpenCode — phrasings like ""have OpenCode do X"", ""delegate this to OpenCode"", ""run it through OpenCode"", or ""use OpenCode to implement/fix/refactor"" — or wants to run a queue of coding tasks through OpenCode while staying the reviewer. Prefer it when the user will review the diff and commit it themselves. DO NOT USE for tasks small enough to do inline, or when the user wants the code written directly without delegating.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/amelnagdy/delegate-skills/opencode-delegate/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/amelnagdy/delegate-skills/opencode-delegate/SKILL.md,1,,1,amelnagdy/delegate-skills,0680f1184ec30f74a87bf0bc9d85fcac4d657ea5,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""opencode-ai"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""1. `opencode --version` succeeds. If not, install (`npm i -g opencode-ai`, or the native installer from""}]",C,"[{""package"": ""opencode-ai"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 2, ""max_severity"": ""CRITICAL"", ""advisory_ids"": [""GHSA-c83v-7274-4vgp"", ""GHSA-vxw4-wv6m-9hhh""]}]"
opencode-runner,"Run coding tasks via opencode using free cloud models. Use when asked to offload work to opencode.ai or run a free model. Don't use for local models (Ollama, LM Studio), Claude/OpenAI calls, or when Claude should do the work itself.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/luongnv89/skills/opencode-runner/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/luongnv89/skills/opencode-runner/SKILL.md,1,,0,,c8ec20a22b2482bcd7afdffe6abced9cceaac097,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""opencode-ai"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""- **opencode installed**: `which opencode` must succeed; install via `npm i -g opencode-ai@latest` or `brew install opencode` if missing""}]",C,"[{""package"": ""opencode-ai"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 2, ""max_severity"": ""CRITICAL"", ""advisory_ids"": [""GHSA-c83v-7274-4vgp"", ""GHSA-vxw4-wv6m-9hhh""]}]"
