reverse-engineering,"Provides reverse engineering techniques. Use when the main job is to understand how a compiled, obfuscated, packed, or virtualized target works before exploiting or solving it, including binaries, APKs, WASM, firmware, custom VMs, bytecode, malware-like loaders, and anti-debug or anti-analysis logic. Do not use it when the vulnerability is already understood and the remaining task is exploitation; use pwn instead. Do not use it for pure web workflows, log or disk forensics, or standalone crypto problems unless reversing the implementation is the real blocker.",NeverSight,learn-skills.dev,194,search_rank=855,search,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev,https://github.com/NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/blob/HEAD/data/skills-md/zhaoxuya520/reverse-skill/reverse-engineering/SKILL.md,NeverSight/learn-skills.dev/data/skills-md/zhaoxuya520/reverse-skill/reverse-engineering/SKILL.md,1,,3,"NeverSight/learn-skills.dev, transilienceai/communitytools",eb8313cc4ec7826e5bba6b97f665a512456a7355,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""frida-tools"", ""ecosystem"": ""pip"", ""install_command"": ""pip install frida-tools angr qiling uncompyle6 capstone lief z3-solver""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""frida-tools"", ""ecosystem"": ""pip"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
