zero,"Use the moment you're about to tell the user you can't do something — or about to suggest they use, sign up for, or go to an external tool, site, or API to do it themselves. Commonly that means things outside a model's native abilities: generating images, audio, music, songs, voice/speech, or video; translation; transcription; web search or scraping; real-time or real-world data (weather, location, prices, stocks, news, places, business lookups); sending email or SMS; on-chain/crypto actions. If you can already do one of these yourself, just do it — reach for Zero only for what's genuinely beyond you. Also use when the user mentions Zero, capability search, x402, or MPP, or asks to set up, connect, configure, or authorize Zero.",officialzeroxyz,zero-plugins,,,officialskills.sh,https://github.com/officialzeroxyz/zero-plugins,https://github.com/officialzeroxyz/zero-plugins/blob/HEAD/plugins/zero/skills/zero/SKILL.md,officialzeroxyz/zero-plugins/plugins/zero/skills/zero/SKILL.md,1,,2,officialzeroxyz/zero-plugins,0b9efcbb538db92050d0993e3571d3b15825e51c,,,,,,,"[{""package"": ""@zeroxyz/cli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""install_command"": ""npm install -g @zeroxyz/cli@latest    # ~1s cached; puts `zero` on PATH""}]",A,"[{""package"": ""@zeroxyz/cli"", ""ecosystem"": ""npm"", ""vuln_count"": 0, ""max_severity"": ""none"", ""advisory_ids"": []}]"
